{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC4 IS IMPLEMENTED — Gerrit change 1305; and the harness changes what AC1 can claim\n\n### 1305 — the operator-visible signal (AC4)\n\n`update_one`'s parent dispatch caught every `set_parent` failure and emitted a `logger.warning` and\nnothing else. 1305 adds a `bridge_alerts` record on each failure arm, keeping warn-and-continue so a\nparent failure still cannot abort the rest of the batch.\n\nDeliberately the EXISTING channel, not a new one: `apply_handlers.record_backstop_failure` already\nwrites `bridge_alerts` for this exact shape of non-fatal-but-real failure, and\n`jira_datacenter/transitions.py:34-49` documents `IllegalTransitionError` being routed there on\npurpose for the same reason. Inventing a second signal would have split the surface an operator has\nto watch.\n\nThree kinds, because the operator's next move differs and collapsing them would say the same words\nfor very different situations:\n * `outbound-parent-unrepresentable` — the deployment cannot hold the relationship at all\n   (`NotImplementedError` from the transport). No retry and no different parent helps.\n * `outbound-parent-rejected` — the 8b25 HTTP 400; Jira refused THIS parent on hierarchy grounds\n   and a different one would be accepted.\n * `outbound-parent-failed` — anything else.\n\nFail-open by construction: an unwritable state directory degrades to a warning rather than failing a\nmutation that would otherwise land. Observability must not cost delivery.\n\n**Evidence.** RED first — 3 of the 5 cells failed against the pre-change tree for the right reasons\n(no record written; no distinct kind; the pass aborting). One cell's assertion was wrong on the\nfirst draft and was FIXED rather than weakened: a parent-ONLY mutation deliberately skips the scalar\nupdate, so it cannot show the rest of the mutation surviving; the fixture now carries a summary too.\n\n**Mutation-checked (AC5), 4 mutations, all killed, each by exactly one cell:**\n\n    M1  drop the alert on the unrepresentable arm      -> 1 failed  (the core cell)\n    M2  collapse the two kinds into one                -> 1 failed  (the distinct-kind cell)\n    M3  alert unconditionally, including on success    -> 1 failed  (the no-alert-on-success cell)\n    M4  remove the fail-open guard in pass_io          -> 1 failed  (the broken-store cell)\n\nM3 is the one that matters most: without that negative cell, an implementation that alerts on every\nparent op passes everything else here and floods the operator's only divergence channel on the happy\npath — worthless as fast as having no signal.\n\nGates: ruff clean, mypy 419 files clean, **2081 passed / 1 xfailed** across\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` + `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler`; 433 passed again after the\nrebase onto current `gerrit/main` (`30c522cde9`).\n\n**Module size, flagged rather than left at the edge.** The first cut put a thin adapter in\n`dispatch_one` and landed at **794/800** — six lines of headroom, the same trap `binding_store` hit\nat 795. I collapsed the adapter into the `pass_io` helper it wrapped (one function instead of two,\nwhich reads better anyway) and it is now **783/800**. `pass_io` is 274.\n\n### THE HARNESS FINDING THAT BEARS ON AC1 — read this before ticking it\n\nRun **30834117797** (main @ `25ead49f3e`, PRE-1302) reported\n`test_outbound_clear_parent_round_trips` RED, which is expected and is this ticket. But it also\nreported **both directions of the SUB-TASK parent path failing**:\n\n * outbound: *\"fields.parent on RBJUUVX-3 is STILL 'RBJUUVX-1' — the parent it had BEFORE the\n   mutation\"* — read back over raw REST, not through the search index.\n * inbound: `get_parent_map` never reflected a reparent within 90s / 45 attempts.\n\nThis ticket's mechanism analysis rests on \"the one child shape DC accepts (sub-task)\". That premise\nis now in doubt: a search-index lag cannot explain a DIRECT field read returning the pre-mutation\nvalue. Filed as [rebar:1a9f-50c0-e7a5-4fda] rather than absorbed here.\n\n**Consequence for AC1** (\"the emit gate and DC's accepted child shape overlap for at least one real\nconfiguration\"): if the sub-task write is also a no-op on DC 8.17.1, the Epic Link path added in\n**1302** is not a second candidate — it is the ONLY one, and AC1 stands or falls on the next harness\nrun. AC1 must NOT be ticked off the unit suite. That is exactly the mistake 1276 made.\n\n1305 also makes the next run more informative: if DC is ERRORING on these writes and the swallow was\nhiding it, an `outbound-parent-*` alert will now appear; if no alert appears, DC returned success and\nlied, which is the accept-and-ignore reading."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785779634741853001,"uuid":"851ab778-239d-4224-aafc-770a3924a0d0"}